rt. Enabling   any of them is the owner's change. - **Every split groups by file ∪ MOSP-graph isomorphism class**   (`learning.fingerprint.union_groups`; certificates in `learning/data/canonical.csv`   and `learning/data/ensemble/results.csv`). - **Nodes, not seconds**, for every hardness statement; seconds beside them.   A censored call (deadline) is a lower bound, never a missing value. - **State the size range every conclusion covers.** The corpus is 6,376   instances at 9–134 customers; the campaign is 37,800 at 10–40; item 02   extends it to 75 and, on the ridge, 100. Nothing below 100 is evidence about   125×125 except through a stated extrapolation. - Every number in a report is regenerated by a command named in that report. - Findings that rest on a handful of instances are re-certified for those   instances (`solve_mosp_exact`, never `solutions_dir=None`) before being written.  - **Compute**: check `pgrep -f benchmarks.recertify`; if it is running, its   cores are not yours. 32 cores total; use up to 16 here. An RTX 5090 with CUDA   is available. Each iteration has a hard 3-hour wall-clock cap enforced by the   driver; budget so the report section and PROGRESS.md are written well inside   it; the two long-running items (03, 04) price their runs with the ridge law   (§14) before starting them and sample if the full run will not fit, saying so.  ## Current Focus `reports/ml_nature_plan_2.md` §3: fourteen items in dependency order. The differential harness comes first because everything after it rests on the answers being sound.  ## Target Problems (in order) See `iterations.md`. Work on exactly ONE unchecked item per iteration.  ## Acceptance Criteria (per item) - [ ] Code lives under `learning/` (or `lean/` for item 12) with a module       docstring saying what question it answers and how to run it; runnable as       `python -m learning.<name>`. - [ ] A section appended to `reports/ml_nature.md` (continuing the numbering,       §15 onwards) with: the question, the method, the baseline, the table(s),       the finding in one paragraph, the size range covered, the kill criterion's       verdict where the plan states one, and the regenerate command. - [ ] `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes (~80 s). New code that computes a       quantity gets at least one test on a tiny hand-checkable instance. A new       flag on the search gets a test that the default is unchanged. - [ ] The item is marked `- [x]` (done) or `- [!]` (blocked, with a reason in       PROGRESS.md) in `iterations.md`. - [ ] No regressions, no changes to solver defaults, nothing written to       `solutions/`. Generated instances and witnesses go under       `learning/data/ensemble/` (committed; keep the total under ~120 MB       apparent, and prefer a manifest of seeds to instance files). DRAT proofs       go under `learning/data/proofs/` which item 03 adds to `.gitignore`; only       their hashes, sizes and checker verdicts are committed.  ## Completion Conditions An item is DONE when either: 1. **Solved**: meets all criteria and the report section is written, OR 2. **Blocked**: documented in PROGRESS.md with the specific blocker. Item 12    (Lean) may end blocked with statements and a gap list; that is a deliverable.  ## Context - **Key files**: `learning/ensemble.py` (the campaign: generation, solving,   refuting, features, certificates; resumable), `learning/node_counts.py`   (`refute`, `refutation_kwargs`: the per-call primitive and the two   configurations), `learning/degeneracy.py` (the lattice oracle,   `optimal_choices`, `count_search`), `learning/graph_story.py` (relabelling   and re-covering primitives from §13), `learning/scale_test.py`   (`fit_scaling`, the corpus node counts in `learning/data/ensemble/scale_nodes.csv`),   `learning/hardness_map.py`, `learning/concentration.py`,   `learning/formula_search.py` (the enumerator for conjecture mining),   `learning/bound_gap.py` (`treewidth_upper_bound`, `describe_instance`, the   ten smallest gap